;Match details

* '''Match 1:''' Surprise win. '''Face vs. heel''' — Ono (Seigigun) vs. Tanaka (c, Cannon Club, World TV Champion). Non-title, but the symbolism was enormous. Tanaka — the traitor who stole the World TV title from Ishida at Episode 5 — underestimated the young lion. Ono, coming off his title shot loss and a week of rest, was sharper than ever. Tanaka targeted the neck again, but Ono had studied the tape. At 11:20, Ono countered a Tanaka powerbomb attempt into a small package — the same move that nearly beat Ishida, now perfected. Three count. The crowd erupted. The young lion had his revenge on the traitor. Post-match: Tanaka was furious, grabbing the title belt and retreating up the ramp. Ono stood in the ring, pointing at the championship — the message was clear: he wants another shot. '''Crowd:''' BIG POP for Ono's entrance. HEAT for Tanaka. "LET'S GO ONO" chants. HEAT at the neck targeting. MEGA POP for the small package — the crowd remembers. "ONO! ONO!" chants after the three count. The young lion is back, and louder than before.
* '''Match 2:''' Destruction match. '''Heel vs. face''' — The Marauder (Unaffiliated) vs. Morita (Seigigun). The Marauder was coming off his first Wednesday night win at Episode 5 — a focused, violent performance. Morita, the rising Seigigun heavyweight, was the test: could The Marauder repeat the destruction? The answer was yes. The wild man was controlled but brutal — power moves, floor brawling, no wasted motion. At 7:45, the running big boot connected for the third consecutive match. The Marauder is becoming a problem. '''Crowd:''' HEAT for The Marauder's entrance. "WHO ARE YOU?" chants. HEAT for the floor brawling. BIG POP for the running big boot. The Marauder stood over Morita post-match — no celebration, just menace. The crowd is starting to respect the violence.
* '''Match 3:''' Upset. '''Face vs. heel''' — Yamamoto (Seigigun) vs. Viggo (Cannon Club, Junior Tag Champion). Yamamoto — the high-flying young fox — had won two consecutive matches. Viggo — El Phantasma, the Mercian junior, half of the Junior Tag champions — was a significant step up in competition. The match was fast and aerial: Yamamoto's speed vs. Viggo's lucha-influenced high-flying. Viggo dominated the middle of the match, but Yamamoto's resilience — and a perfectly timed springboard DDT at 10:15 — gave the young gun the surprise win. The Cannon Club's junior division took another hit. '''Crowd:''' POP for Yamamoto. HEAT for Viggo. "YAMAMOTO" chants. BIG POP for the springboard DDT. The young guns are winning the war of attrition.
* '''Match 4:''' Tag title match. '''Heel vs. tweener/face''' — The Usos (c, Cannon Club) vs. Reyes & Kimura (CHAOS), ended by disqualification. The final confrontation before Island Invasion. The Usos' experience and tag-team chemistry were on display, but Reyes and Kimura — the Cobra and the Wind — were relentless. The match broke down in the final minutes: Reyes snapped and grabbed a steel chair, swinging at Tama Uso. The referee called for the bell at 16:30. The Usos retain by DQ, but the message was sent — Reyes and Kimura are willing to cross the line to take the titles. Post-match: Reyes and Kimura brawled with the Usos, chairs and all, until officials separated them. The Island Invasion tag title match is now personal. '''Crowd:''' HEAT for the Usos. POP for Reyes & Kimura. "COBRA" chants. HEAT at the chair shot. BIG POP for the post-match brawl. The crowd is firmly behind the challengers.
* '''Match 5:''' Tag team grudge match. '''Face vs. heel''' — Kawada & Takagi (CHAOS) vs. Big Stan & Diallo (Cannon Club). A rematch from Episode 5, where Kawada and Takagi defeated Big Stan and Diallo. This time, the stakes were higher — CHAOS wanted to send a message before Island Invasion, and the Cannon Club power team needed to prove it could win. The match was a war of strikes and power. Big Stan's size was a factor, but Kawada's brainbuster on Diallo at 12:50 ended it — CHAOS wins again. The Cannon Club's mid-card power team has now lost twice in two weeks. '''Crowd:''' POP for CHAOS. HEAT for the Cannon Club. "KAWADA" chants. GASPS at Big Stan's body slam on Takagi. BIG POP for the brainbuster finish. The Cannon Club's depth is cracking.
* '''Match 6:''' Strong Openweight title match. '''Face vs. heel''' — Taumafa (c, Independent) vs. Malo (Cannon Club). Family vs. family. Kengo sent his brother Malo to test the independent Strong Openweight Champion — a more personal challenge than Big Stan. The match was heated and physical, with Malo targeting Taumafa's lower back and using underhanded tactics. Taumafa fought through the pain, hitting the Samoan Spike at 15:10 to retain. Post-match: Taumafa took the mic and challenged Kengo directly — "Send yourself next time." Kengo, watching from the ramp, smiled. The family war is coming to the Island Invasion Tour. '''Crowd:''' MEGA POP for Taumafa. NUCLEAR HEAT for Malo. "TAUMAFA" chants. BIG POP for the Samoan Spike. Taumafa's challenge drew a mixed reaction — the crowd wants Kengo in the ring.
* '''Match 7:''' IC title match. '''Heel vs. face''' — Vance (c, Cannon Club) vs. Kuroki (Seigigun). Vance's fifth consecutive match-of-the-night candidate — and the most dramatic. The technical masterpiece: Vance's cool precision vs. Kuroki's strong-style brutality. The two former Kuroshio rivals (Vance was never in Kuroshio, but Kuroki was) told a story of respect and violence. Kuroki kicked out of the Drill Driver at 2.5. Vance kicked out of the Black Iron Clothesline at 2.5. The crowd was on its feet. At 19:45, Vance had Kuroki locked in the Drill Driver position for the finish — and then the lights cut. A single spotlight hit the entrance ramp. A man stood there: muscular, bearded, wearing black compression gear with heavy leather trousers — a [[Balisca|Baliscan]] oil wrestler. The crowd went silent. He walked to the ring, slid inside, and without a word attacked both Vance and Kuroki. The referee called for the bell — no contest. The man grabbed a microphone and spoke in heavily accented Mercian: ''"My name is Jusuf Muntasir. In Balisca, we call this mosaraza. You call it pro wrestling. I call it a lie."'' He dropped the mic and left both men lying. '''Crowd:''' HEAT for Vance's entrance. POP for Kuroki. "THIS IS AWESOME" chants. MEGA POP for the Drill Driver kick-out. GASPS at the Black Iron Clothesline kick-out. SILENCE when the lights cut. CONFUSION when Jusuf appeared. HEAT when he attacked both men. The crowd didn't know what to make of him — until he spoke. Then: nuclear heat. The interruption was shocking. Vance's fifth MOTN ended in chaos.
* '''Match 8:''' Kuroshio fracture match. '''Tweener vs. face''' — KAZUKI (Independent) vs. Maeda (Seigigun). The mediator vs. the man who no longer wants to be mediated. Maeda came out first, microphone in hand, begging KAZUKI to talk. KAZUKI's music hit. He walked to the ring, looked at Maeda, and took the mic: ''"There is nothing to talk about."'' The match was fast and emotional — KAZUKI's aerial offense vs. Maeda's speed and heart. Maeda nearly won with the Speed Star Press, but KAZUKI kicked out. At 17:30, the Twin Star Press ended it. KAZUKI defeated his former Kuroshio brother. Post-match: KAZUKI did not celebrate. He looked down at Maeda, then at the ramp. The message was for Leoni. '''Crowd:''' BIG POP for Maeda's entrance. MEGA POP for KAZUKI's entrance. "KUROSHIO" chants — the last time that chant would mean anything. GASPS at the Speed Star Press kick-out. MEGA POP for the Twin Star Press. Silence after the match. The bond is breaking.
* '''Match 9:''' Main event. '''Face vs. heel''' — Leoni Masua vs. Kengo Vaiahi. Non-title, but the stakes were everything. Kengo — the Cannon Club leader, Leoni's cousin, the man who declared war on the Vaiahi family. Leoni — the IGO Heavyweight Champion, the Tribal Chief, two weeks from defending against KAZUKI. The match was a brawl from the opening bell. Kengo targeted Leoni's ribs, trying to soften him for Island Invasion. Leoni fought back with the Spear of Fangatapu attempt, but Kengo rolled out of the ring. The match spilled to the floor. At 18:40, Leoni had Kengo down on the outside and was about to throw him back in — when KAZUKI's music hit. The Shooting Star walked to the ring, slowly, deliberately. Leoni turned to face him. KAZUKI didn't speak. He lunged at Leoni, and the two brawled on the floor. The referee counted both men out — Kengo won by countout, rolling back into the ring at the last second, smiling. The cheekiest win of his career. But the night wasn't over. Maeda ran out to separate Leoni and KAZUKI. Kuroki ran out to help Maeda. The four former Kuroshio members were in the ring together for the first time since Episode 1 — and they brawled. Leoni and Kuroki vs. KAZUKI and Maeda? No — it was every man for himself. KAZUKI attacked Maeda. Leoni attacked KAZUKI. Kuroki tried to stop Leoni, then attacked KAZUKI. Officials stormed the ring. The four men were separated, but the image was clear: Kuroshio was dead. '''Crowd:''' NUCLEAR POP for Leoni's entrance. NUCLEAR HEAT for Kengo's entrance. "TRIBAL CHIEF" chants. HEAT for Kengo's rib targeting. MEGA POP for the Spear attempt. TENSION when KAZUKI's music hit. MIXED reaction as KAZUKI attacked Leoni. HEAT for Kengo's countout win. NUCLEAR POP for the Kuroshio brawl. "KUROSHIO" chants turned to confusion, then silence. The bond is broken.

== Post-match segment: The End of Kuroshio ==

=== Kengo's gloating ===

The bell rings. Kengo Vaiahi is in the ring, having won by countout. He has a microphone. He's smiling — not cold, not calculating, genuinely amused.

:''"That's how you beat a chief. You don't pin him. You don't submit him. You let his own family tear him apart."'' — NUCLEAR HEAT

:''"Leoni. KAZUKI. Maeda. Kuroki. The Black Tide. The brotherhood. The bond. Look at them. They can't even stand in the same ring without killing each other. And at Fangatapu, the Chief has to face the Shooting Star — alone. No Maeda. No Kuroki. No Kuroshio. Just Leoni and the man who hates him most."'' — HEAT

:''"The Cannon Club doesn't need to break the Chief. The Chief's own brothers already did."''

Kengo drops the mic and backs up the ramp, flanked by Malo and Marcus Vance. Vance is still selling the Jusuf attack, holding his ribs.

=== The four men in the ring ===

In the ring: Leoni Masua, Ryohei Maeda, KAZUKI, and Daigo Kuroki. Officials are trying to separate them. The crowd is silent, then begins to chant '''KUROSHIO''' — but the chant dies quickly. The four men are not a team anymore.

Maeda takes the mic. His voice is broken:

:''"We were Kuroshio. We were the Black Tide. And now —"''

KAZUKI snatches the mic from Maeda's hand.

:''"And now nothing. You want to save something that is already dead. I don't need Kuroshio. I don't need you. I need that title. And in two weeks, I take it from the Chief."'' — HUGE POP, mixed with heat

KAZUKI drops the mic and walks out of the ring through the crowd. He does not look back.

Leoni picks up the mic. He looks at Maeda, then at Kuroki.

:''"The bond is gone. But the spear is still here. Fangatapu. The Chief walks in champion. The Chief walks out champion."'' — HUGE POP

Kuroki takes the mic last. He looks at the three men around him.

:''"Kuroshio is dead. But I am not. Seigigun is not. And at Fangatapu, we fight."'' — POP

The four men leave through separate exits. The Black Tide is over.

=== Backstage: Leoni watches Vance ===

In a backstage segment, Leoni Masua stands in front of a monitor, watching replay of the Jusuf Muntasir attack on Marcus Vance. His arms are crossed. He doesn't smile.

:''"The Cannon Club left him alone out there. No Kengo. No Malo. No Usos. They watched him get attacked."'' — Pause. — ''"Marcus Vance is a cold man. But even a cold man can get lonely. Keep your eye on him. Something is changing."''

The segment ends with Leoni walking away. The implication is clear: the Tribal Chief sees the shift in Vance before Vance sees it himself.

